naomi osaka withdraws from the french  open  citing depression and social anxiety  now stars like serena williams billie  jean king  russell wilson and steph curry are  speaking out to support her  the tennis star shared her decision to  exit the tournament on twitter monday  just days after she made headlines for  announcing she would not be  participating in press conferences at  the french open  which began on sunday she wrote at the  time that she believed the practice was  harmful to athletes mental health  and on monday she tweeted in part quote  i think now the best thing for the  tournament the other players and my  well-being is that i withdraw so that  everyone can get back to focusing on the  tennis going on in paris  the 23 year old athlete continued  revealing that she has suffered from  long bouts of depression  since the u.s open in 2018 and has had a  really hard time coping with that  she explained that she also has social  anxiety and talking to the press  is tough for her quote i am not a  natural public speaker and get huge  waves of anxiety before i speak to the  world's media  i get really nervous and find it  stressful to always try to engage and  give you the best answers i can  naomi continued writing that she was  already feeling vulnerable and  anxious and viewed skipping press  conferences as an act of self-care  she explained that she made the  announcement that she wouldn't be doing  press preemptively  because she feels the rules are outdated  in parts and when the time is right  she says she wants to work with the tour  to discuss ways to make things better  for the players  the press and fans  and there is part of the difference in  this match osaka sees a chance  following naomi's decision to withdraw  the president of the french tennis  federation said in a statement to  journalists published by the washington  post  that they are sorry and sad for naomi  and added that while her decision to  withdraw was unfortunate  they're also wishing her the quickest  possible recovery  and they are looking forward to having  naomi in the tournament next year  ahead of her public statement the  tournament organization announced on  sunday  that naomi was fined fifteen thousand  dollars after not appearing at a press  conference at the french open  adding that the four-time grand slam  winner could face harsher penalties if  she continued to refuse to speak to the  media following her monday announcement  to withdraw  naomi received a ton of support from  some of her famous fans and fellow  athletes  serena williams who is competing in this  year's french open  addressed the news at a post-match press  conference following her round one  victory  i feel for naomi i feel like  i wish i could give her a hug because i  know what it's like like i said i've  been in those positions  we have different personalities and  people are different  not everyone is the same um i'm thick  you know other people are thin so um  everyone is different and everyone  handles things differently  so you know you just have to  let her handle it the way she wants to  in the best way that she thinks she can  tennis legend martina navratilova  tweeted that she hopes naomi will be  okay  adding quote this is about more than  doing or not doing a press conference  good luck naomi we are all pulling for  you  billie jean king a 39 grand slam winner  and tennis icon praised naomi as  incredibly brave for revealing her truth  and encouraged everyone to give her time  and space  athletes from other sports have shared  their love and support as well  nfl star russell wilson retweeted  naomi's statement  writing we are with you naomi hashtag  courage  olympic gymnast lori hernandez applauded  naomi for speaking up  tweeting that she's proud of her for  putting her foot down  adding quote your mental health matters  and should always come first  meanwhile nba star steph curry tweeted  you shouldn't ever have to make a  decision like this  but so damn impressive taking the high  road when the powers that be  don't protect their own major respect
 

